<?php
/**
 * "حسابي" — the account information card, read state. Figma 562:10229.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHAT REPLACED WHAT
 * ===========================================================================
 * This was core's two-box dashboard with a Spartrak patch on the email line.
 * It is now the card Figma draws: a 103px header carrying the page's heading
 * and its one action, and a body of three labelled values.
 *
 * The two boxes it dropped are not lost. The newsletter box is a destination
 * Figma removed from the rail (see customer_account.xml) and its page still
 * works; the address box has a page of its own at customer/address.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * WHY THE VALUES ARE <p> AND NOT DISABLED <input>
 * ===========================================================================
 * Figma draws them inside input-shaped boxes, and the temptation is to render
 * readonly inputs so the shape comes for free. They are not inputs: nothing
 * here submits, nothing here is focusable, and a readonly input in a tab order
 * that leads nowhere is a worse experience for a keyboard user than static
 * text. The box is drawn by the same `__band` wrapper the edit form uses, so
 * the two states share one 48px frame; what differs is its fill (this state
 * adds the `display` modifier, bg/surface-subtle per 562:16397, against the
 * component's white default) and what sits inside it.
 *
 * It is also the cheaper DOM — three <p> against three <input> plus a <form>
 * that would never post.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE MISSING EMAIL
 * ===========================================================================
 * A phone-registered customer has a synthesised address in customer_entity
 * which must never be shown (Spartrak_CustomerAuth's PlaceholderEmail).
 * Profile::getEmail() returns null for those rows and the field prints "لم يتم
 * إضافته" in the muted ramp instead.
 *
 * The standalone "[Add email]" link the previous revision of this template
 * carried is folded into the card's own تعديل action, which lands on exactly
 * the form that link pointed at. Two controls one line apart, leading to the
 * same page, is not an affordance — it is a decision the shopper has to make
 * twice.
 *
 * ===========================================================================
 * THE PHONE IS READ-ONLY IN BOTH STATES
 * ===========================================================================
 * Deliberate, and the one place this card does not do what its edit state
 * appears to offer. The phone number IS the sign-in identifier on this
 * storefront (Spartrak_CustomerAuth), it is uniquely indexed, and the only
 * verified paths that touch it are signup and password reset —
 * Otp\Purpose has no third value. Letting it be changed from a form with no
 * verification step would let a shopper point their own login at a number they
 * do not control, and there is no Figma frame for a change-phone flow to build
 * instead. Flagged rather than faked.
 *
 * @var \Magento\Customer\Block\Account\Dashboard\Info $block
 * @var \Magento\Framework\Escaper $escaper
 */

use Spartrak\CustomerAccount\ViewModel\Profile;

/** @var Profile|null $profile */
$profile = $block->getData('profile');
$email = $profile?->getEmail();
?>
<div class="spartrak-account-card">
    <div class="spartrak-account-card__header">
        <div class="spartrak-account-card__heading">
            <h1 class="spartrak-account-card__title"><?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('My account')) ?></h1>
            <p class="spartrak-account-card__subtitle">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(
                    __('Edit or complete your account details, including how your data is secured.')
                ) ?>
            </p>
        </div>
        <a class="spartrak-account-card__action"
           href="<?= $escaper->escapeUrl($block->getUrl('customer/account/edit')) ?>">
            <span class="spartrak-account-card__action-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span><?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Edit')) ?></span>
        </a>
    </div>

    <div class="spartrak-account-card__body">
        <div class="spartrak-account-field">
            <span class="spartrak-account-field__label" id="spartrak-account-name-label">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('User name')) ?>
            </span>
            <!--
              The 48px band, on all three fields. Figma 562:16395 / 562:16465
              / 562:16476 are the same "Text Input" component three times over
              — the read state never differs from the edit state (562:17237)
              in whether there is a box, only in its fill and its contents.
              `--display` is that fill: bg/surface-subtle, measured on
              562:16397, against 821:17288's white for the editable instance.
            -->
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band spartrak-account-field__band--display">
                <p class="spartrak-account-field__value" aria-labelledby="spartrak-account-name-label">
                    <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($profile?->getName() ?? '') ?>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spartrak-account-field">
            <span class="spartrak-account-field__label" id="spartrak-account-email-label">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Email address')) ?>
            </span>
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band spartrak-account-field__band--display">
                <p class="spartrak-account-field__value<?= $email === null
                        ? ' spartrak-account-field__value--empty'
                        : '' ?>"
                   aria-labelledby="spartrak-account-email-label">
                    <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($email ?? __('Not added')) ?>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="spartrak-account-field">
            <span class="spartrak-account-field__label" id="spartrak-account-phone-label">
                <?= $escaper->escapeHtml(__('Phone number')) ?>
            </span>
            <!--
              One bordered band holding two segments, exactly as Figma draws it
              (562:16478): the dialling code in its own boxed segment at the
              reading start, the number beside it. DOM order is dial then
              number, so an RTL row puts the code on the right and an LTR one
              puts it on the left, with no second rule.
            -->
            <div class="spartrak-account-field__band spartrak-account-field__band--display">
                <span class="spartrak-account-field__dial"><?= $escaper->escapeHtml(
                    $profile?->getPhoneDialCode() ?? ''
                ) ?></span>
                <p class="spartrak-account-field__value" aria-labelledby="spartrak-account-phone-label">
                    <?= $escaper->escapeHtml($profile?->getPhoneNational() ?? '') ?>
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <?= $block->getChildHtml('customer.account.dashboard.info.extra') ?>
        <?= $block->getChildHtml('additional_blocks') ?>
    </div>
</div>
